WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.160
- [Narrator] The
kouign-amann is a specialty

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:05.040
of Northern France. Derived
from the Breton words

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:09.120
for butter and cake, the ratio
for this pastry is special.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.350
It's buttery.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:14.254
In fact, it's 30 percent
butter and 30 percent sugar.

00:00:14.254 --> 00:00:17.587
(mellow, playful music)

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:22.220
Welcome to Douarnenez,
a city with a population

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:25.480
of around 15,000; this small coastal town

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.160
has a few main attractions,

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.240
including touring the coastlines,

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:31.750
visiting the Port Museum,
and seeing the Chapelle

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:34.180
of Saint-Michel.
(upbeat, playful music)

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.340
But that's not why we're here.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:38.530
We are here to meet Thierry Lucas,

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:40.040
the man to talk to when you want

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:43.011
a truly authentic kouign-amann pastry.

00:00:43.011 --> 00:00:47.594
(Thierry speaks in a foreign language)

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:54.040
Legend goes a baker ran
out of goods in their shop

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:55.716
and had to whip up something quickly.

00:00:55.716 --> 00:01:00.299
(Thierry speaks in a foreign language)

00:01:09.337 --> 00:01:11.940
The pastry has only a
few simple ingredients,

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:14.378
but don't let that fool you.
(upbeat music)

00:01:14.378 --> 00:01:18.961
(Thierry speaks in a foreign language)

00:01:44.018 --> 00:01:45.864
(upbeat music)

00:01:45.864 --> 00:01:50.447
(Thierry speaks in a foreign language)

00:01:57.882 --> 00:01:59.300
(upbeat music)

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:00.660
It's definitely a treat,

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:03.159
probably not something
you'd eat every day.

00:02:03.159 --> 00:02:07.742
(Thierry speaks in a foreign language)

00:02:21.062 --> 00:02:24.894
Not to have the last word,
but obviously, we tried it.

00:02:24.894 --> 00:02:26.230
Bon appetite!
- Bon appetite.

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:27.730
- And I think our face says it all.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:30.293
And also, this spontaneous remark.

00:02:30.293 --> 00:02:32.332
Oh my God, that's so buttery.

00:02:32.332 --> 00:02:35.670
(man speaks in foreign language)

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:37.270
- Ten out of 10, would recommend.

00:02:38.676 --> 00:02:39.509
Whoa.

00:02:41.219 --> 00:02:43.719
(light music)

